---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About"><section class="section"><div class="container page"><p class="eyebrow">About the group</p><h1>Distinct restaurants, shared standards.</h1><p class="lede">Asia Major Eateries is built as a restaurant group rather than a single-location website. The guest-facing brand can stay warm and local while shared systems keep hours, menus, prices, availability, reservations and operations consistent.</p></div></section><section class="section band"><div class="container values"><article><h2>Local first</h2><p>Every location has its own hours, services, menu state and neighborhood context.</p></article><article><h2>Useful truth</h2><p>Live information carries freshness and source metadata instead of presenting stale data as current.</p></article><article><h2>Operational rigor</h2><p>Typed contracts and a hardened data model support the hospitality layer without leaking complexity to guests.</p></article></div></section></BaseLayout>
<style>.page{display:grid;gap:28px}.band{background:var(--paper2)}.values{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:32px}.values article{display:grid;gap:14px}.values p{color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:760px){.values{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
